{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-explainer-about-australian-cafe-culture-and-business-culture-teach-how-people-can-be-ca/audio/main-19e89c10fd18.mp3","durationSec":221.568,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.02,"text":"An Australian cafe is not only a place to buy coffee."},{"start":3.64,"end":6.98,"text":"People may meet, talk, read, or take a short break there."},{"start":7.52,"end":9.92,"text":"A regular is a customer who comes back often."},{"start":9.92,"end":13.72,"text":"Staff may remember the person’s order and ask, “The usual?”"},{"start":14.38,"end":17.38,"text":"This sounds casual, but it also shows careful service."},{"start":18.08,"end":20.72,"text":"A customer may say, “Can I get a flat white?”"},{"start":21.44,"end":25.58,"text":"A flat white has espresso, steamed milk, and a thin layer of soft foam."},{"start":25.9,"end":29.14,"text":"In Australia, it often comes in a ceramic cup."},{"start":29.14,"end":34.22,"text":"Coffee remained part of daily life in Australia in 2026."},{"start":34.88,"end":43.04,"text":"The cafe and coffee shop industry had 27,821 businesses and a market size of $15.9 billion."},{"start":44.16,"end":47.2,"text":"However, people watched their spending more carefully."},{"start":47.78,"end":51.8,"text":"In June 2026, the average cup cost $4.69."},{"start":52.52,"end":59.92,"text":"Cafe spending fell 1.4% from the year before, and 83% of surveyed cafe operators noticed fewer visits."},{"start":60.72,"end":64.04,"text":"Still, 93% of cafe spending happened in person."},{"start":65.48,"end":71.38,"text":"This gives a real business picture: many people still liked visiting their local cafe, but some went less often."},{"start":71.38,"end":74.86,"text":"Casual language does not mean careless work."},{"start":75.66,"end":78.48,"text":"Think about two things: style and standard."},{"start":79.26,"end":84.9,"text":"The style can be friendly and relaxed, while the standard for coffee, time, and service can stay high."},{"start":85.72,"end":88.36,"text":"A customer may ask directly, “How long will it take?”"},{"start":88.98,"end":91.58,"text":"A plain complaint may be, “This coffee is cold.”"},{"start":92.42,"end":95.54,"text":"These words can sound strong, but they clearly show the problem."},{"start":96.28,"end":99.4,"text":"Good business service focuses on the problem and fixes it."},{"start":99.82,"end":106.94,"text":"Australian cafe culture often values drink quality more than loud marketing, so exaggerated claims may create less trust."},{"start":108.16,"end":112.24,"text":"Cafe business also sits inside a larger relationship between Australia and Japan."},{"start":112.76,"end":119.66,"text":"In 2025, Japan was Australia’s second-largest partner for merchandise and services exports, worth $65.1 billion."},{"start":120.52,"end":124.24,"text":"It was the third-largest partner for imports, worth $32.4 billion."},{"start":125.24,"end":126.66,"text":"Travel was also strong."},{"start":127.14,"end":132.48,"text":"During 2025, 1,058,300 Australian travellers visited Japan."},{"start":133.1,"end":138.14,"text":"This was the first year the number passed one million, and it was 15% higher than in 2024."},{"start":138.8,"end":144.3,"text":"These trade and travel links help people meet new products, food ideas, and ways of doing business."},{"start":144.9,"end":150.22,"text":"Imagine an unnamed cafe in Japan offering a black latte made with bamboo charcoal powder."},{"start":151.24,"end":155.06,"text":"Bamboo charcoal can give a drink a surprising black colour."},{"start":155.06,"end":162.34,"text":"The cafe may also explain Binchotan, a high-quality white charcoal made for a long time in Wakayama from ubame oak."},{"start":163,"end":164.9,"text":"The business should be clear about the product."},{"start":165.3,"end":170.4,"text":"It can describe the colour, taste, and ingredients without calling the drink a miracle health product."},{"start":171.2,"end":176.08,"text":"Some charcoal health claims have weak evidence, and activated charcoal can bind to medicines."},{"start":176.08,"end":180.48,"text":"Customers may like the creative look, but honest information builds trust."},{"start":180.48,"end":184.6,"text":"Picture an unnamed family workshop making Japanese roof tiles."},{"start":185.42,"end":187.62,"text":"These fired-clay tiles are called kawara."},{"start":188.3,"end":193.78,"text":"They came to Japan from Baekche during the sixth century and were first used on temples and government buildings."},{"start":194.24,"end":199.16,"text":"The Kawara Museum in Omihachiman now shows local tile history and production."},{"start":199.94,"end":205,"text":"The family may make an onigawara, a roof ornament with a fierce face or beast."},{"start":205.98,"end":215.3,"text":"Instead of saying, “Our work is the best in the world,” they can show the clay, firing process, strong finished tile, and family skill."},{"start":216.18,"end":220.92,"text":"Like a good cafe, the workshop can feel friendly while taking quality seriously."}],"words":[{"text":"An","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"Australian","start":0.18,"end":0.64},{"text":"cafe","start":0.64,"end":0.94},{"text":"is","start":0.94,"end":1.34},{"text":"not","start":1.34,"end":1.58},{"text":"only","start":1.58,"end":1.88},{"text":"a","start":1.88,"end":2.02},{"text":"place","start":2.02,"end":2.2},{"text":"to","start":2.2,"end":2.42},{"text":"buy","start":2.42,"end":2.56},{"text":"coffee","start":2.56,"end":3.02},{"text":"People","start":3.64,"end":3.9},{"text":"may","start":3.9,"end":4.08},{"text":"meet","start":4.08,"end":4.4},{"text":"talk","start":4.6,"end":5},{"text":"read","start":5.24,"end":5.58},{"text":"or","start":5.76,"end":5.92},{"text":"take","start":5.92,"end":6.08},{"text":"a","start":6.08,"end":6.24},{"text":"short","start":6.24,"end":6.42},{"text":"break","start":6.42,"end":6.68},{"text":"there","start":6.68,"end":6.98},{"text":"A","start":7.52,"end":7.62},{"text":"regula